# layout.fk: mall.fk's machines with no @(x, y) hints, so `fk layout` places them. Plot 34x44.
# An instance without a hint is unplaced until `fk layout` places it: the instances move under a
# routability potential (short, uncrowded belts between them), and `--write` puts the hints into
# this file; then `fk build --to report_checks` routes it like any other.
# Run:  fk layout layout.fk --plot 34x44       fk layout layout.fk --plot 34x44 --write
# Expect: `layout layout: 11 instances, 11 placed now, 0 kept, 0 fixed; 8 nets; frame 34x44 (--plot)`,
# one source line per instance with its new `@(x, y)`, then `estimated belts 62 -> 4 over 8 nets`.
fein  = Chest<requester, item=iron-plate, rate=2/s>
cuin  = Chest<requester, item=copper-plate, rate=1/s>
gear  = Assembler<recipe=iron-gear-wheel>
belt  = Assembler<recipe=transport-belt>
ins   = Assembler<recipe=inserter>
cable = Assembler<recipe=copper-cable>
circ  = Assembler<recipe=electronic-circuit>
pipe  = AsmRow<n=2, recipe=pipe>
bbox  = Chest<provider, limit=4>
ibox  = Chest<provider, limit=4>
pbox  = Chest<provider, limit=4>

net fe:    fein -> gear, circ, belt, ins, pipe
net cu:    cuin -> cable
net gears: gear -> belt, ins
net cab:   cable -> circ
net circs: circ -> ins
net belts: belt -> bbox
net inss:  ins -> ibox
net pipes: pipe -> pbox
